{"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"title":"Binary decision diagrams","anchor":"Binary-decision-diagrams","identifiers":["doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram"]},{"title":"Zero-suppressed decision diagrams","anchor":"Zero-suppressed-decision-diagrams","identifiers":["doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is a table of reduced ordered binary decision diagrams (Bryant,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"1986). Each function is a directed acyclic graph whose vertices test variables in index order,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with a low child for the variable false and a high child for true, down to the constants. No two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices test the same variable with the same children, and none has equal children, so each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"function has exactly one root, and checking whether two functions are equal is comparing roots."}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import DecisionDiagrams","","var diagram = BinaryDecisionDiagram(variableCount: 3)","let x0 = diagram.variable(0), x1 = diagram.variable(1), x2 = diagram.variable(2)","let f = diagram.or(diagram.and(x0, x1), x2)   \/\/ x0 ∧ x1 ∨ x2","diagram.satisfyingAssignmentCount(of: f)       \/\/ 5","diagram.anySatisfyingAssignment(of: f)         \/\/ [false, false, true]"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The diagram of "},{"code":"f","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" has five vertices: three tests and the two constants. Following the low edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"means the variable is false, the high edge that it is true."}]},{"type":"table","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Vertex"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Tests"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Low child"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"High child","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"root"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x0"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"the test of ","type":"text"},{"code":"x2","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"the test of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x1"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"x1","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"the test of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x2"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"true"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"x2","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"false"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"true","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The test of ","type":"text"},{"code":"x2","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is shared: ","type":"text"},{"code":"x0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" false and ","type":"text"},{"code":"x0 ∧ ¬x1","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" both leave ","type":"text"},{"code":"f","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" equal to ","type":"text"},{"code":"x2","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so both lead","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to the one vertex that stands for it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Functions combine under any of the sixteen binary operators with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/apply(_:_:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" in O(|"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"f","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":"| |"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"g"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":"|), through a computed table of results"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"already found. "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/restrict(_:variable:to:)"},{"type":"text","text":" fixes a variable, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/exists(_:in:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/forall(_:in:)"},{"type":"text","text":" quantify"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"over variables. The table’s vertices are a "},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/graphView-swift.property"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so Grafluent’s traversals and drawings run over a function’s diagram from its root."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram","isActive":true},{"text":" is a table of families of sets (Minato, 1993). Its vertices","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"test elements in index order, with a low child for the sets without the element and a high child","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for those with it. In place of the rule that removes a vertex with equal children, it removes one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whose high child is the empty family, so an element no set contains never appears in a diagram,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and a sparse family over many elements stays small.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["var diagram = ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram(elementCount: 3)","let f = diagram.family([[0, 1], [1, 2], [2]])","diagram.count(of: f)                                 \/\/ 3","diagram.minimalSets(of: diagram.including(2, in: f)) \/\/ {{2}}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Families combine by ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram\/union(_:_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram\/intersection(_:_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram\/subtracting(_:from:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", and set by set by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram\/join(_:_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram\/meet(_:_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram\/setsView(of:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" lists a family’s sets, and its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram\/graphView-swift.property","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" is a ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" like the binary diagram’s.","type":"text"}]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/decisiondiagrams"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"abstract":[{"text":"Canonical diagrams of Boolean functions and families of sets.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"role":"collection","modules":[{"name":"DecisionDiagrams"}],"externalID":"DecisionDiagrams","symbolKind":"module","title":"DecisionDiagrams","roleHeading":"Framework"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams"},"references":{"doc://DecisionDiagrams/documentation/DecisionDiagrams/BinaryDecisionDiagram/graphView-swift.property":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"graphView","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BinaryDecisionDiagram","preciseIdentifier":"s:16DecisionDiagrams06BinaryA7DiagramV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"GraphView","preciseIdentifier":"s:16DecisionDiagrams06BinaryA7DiagramV9GraphViewV","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/graphView-swift.property","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The table’s vertices as a directed acyclic graph: a vertex per diagram vertex, 0 the false"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"constant and 1 the true one, and from each other vertex a low edge and a high edge, which"},{"ty